   "id": 504367,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Petunias can be blue, red, or violet. When a blue flower is crossed with a red flower, all the resulting flowers are violet. Two violet petunias are crossed. Which is the most probable result of the cross?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 992057,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"75\\%\">75\\%</span> of the flowers are blue and <span data-math=\"25\\%\">25\\%</span> of the flowers are red."
    },
    {
     "id": 992058,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"50\\%\">50\\%</span> of the flowers are blue and <span data-math=\"50\\%\">50\\%</span> of the flowers are red."
    },
    {
     "id": 992059,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"75\\%\">75\\%</span> of the flowers are red and <span data-math=\"25\\%\">25\\%</span> are blue."
    },
    {
     "id": 992060,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"25\\%\">25\\%</span> of the flowers are blue, <span data-math=\"50\\%\">50\\%</span> of the flowers are violet, and <span data-math=\"25\\%\">25\\%</span> of the flowers are red."
    }
